2.2 GMAC and network stack
--------------------------
The GMAC0 board bring-up (SunxiGmacDxe), the DesignWare MAC SNP driver
(DwEmacSnpDxe), the network-stack configuration driver
(NetworkStackConfigDxe), the minimal EFI_RNG_PROTOCOL provider
(SunxiRngDxe) and A733ClockLib are ported from
github.com/vehoelite/edk2-a733 (edk2-allwinner), BSD-2-Clause-Patent,
Copyright (c) 2026 carpi-os contributors; DwEmacSnpDxe also carries the
original Copyright (c) 2012-2014 ARM Limited.  SunxiRngDxe exists only
because DxeNetLib's Depex requires gEfiRngProtocolGuid; it is seeded from
the arch timer and is not a hardware TRNG.  The GPIO and TWI calls in
SunxiGmacDxe were adapted to this tree's A733GpioLib and A733TwiLib; the
register programming and the UEFI interfaces are unchanged.

3. Register-level facts established against another firmware
-----------------------------------------------------------
Four values in the SPI-NOR backend are not what the vendor manual alone
gives: the pads carry SPI0 as pin function 5 (the manual's port table reads as
3), the controller's CCR, SAMP_DL and FCR need 2 / 0x5000 / 0x00200140 to
produce a clock at all, and a command is two bursts rather than one
full-duplex burst.  Each was established by failing on hardware with the
manual's reading and then cross-checking against a *different firmware running
on the same board* - a source of facts about this silicon, not of code.  No
source text, comment or structure was taken from it or from any vendor
driver; the implementation was written against those facts and the evidence
for each value is recorded next to it in the driver.

The USB work rests on the same footing, and the list is longer because the
manual is thinner there:

  - the USB0/USB1 CCU words outside the manual's USB clock chapter (the keyed
    AHB master gate, CLK_MSI_LITE2, CLK_RES_DCAP_24M, the pll-peri0 output
    gates) - without them the PHY window at 0x04101800 does not take a write
    and the PHY is not powered (A733Ccu.h);
  - the HCI PHY recipe: the passby word 0x00008A01 (bits 15, 11, 9, 8 and 0),
    of which the ULPI-bypass bit is what joins the PHY's UTMI port to the
    controller at all, plus the tune and UTMI control words (A733Usb.h);
  - the wrapper's OTG control (ISCR) pull-up enables at bits 17:16, which the
    manual marks reserved, and the PHYCTL writes the manual describes only
    partly (A733Musb.h);
  - POWER as a single write of HSENAB | SOFTCONN | SUSPENDM with nothing
    cleared afterwards (A733Musb.h, POWER);
  - the bulk endpoint FIFO layout: the vendor's EP1 TX at byte 1124 and EP2 RX
    at byte 100, the latter widened here to eight packets at byte 2048
    (A733Musb.h);
  - the controller's interrupt as GIC SPI 156 / INTID 188, which the platform's
    device tree contradicts (it reuses the A523's SPI 29) and which the closed
    firmware and the reference driver both agree on (A733MusbDeviceDxe.c);
  - and the negative result that shapes the bulk path: the MUSB core's own DMA
    window (0x500/0x504, 0x540 + 0x10n) does not answer on this die, and the
    SoC's DMAC - the manual's answer, DRQ ports 27..34 for USB0's device
    endpoints - reads as secure (SEC = 0), so no normal-world transfer can be
    programmed (A733Musb.h, A733Dmac.h).  A733DmacLib implements that block
    anyway, from the manual's chapter 13 alone, because the block exists and
    because the day BL31 opens it the driver is already written.

Each of those was established by watching the manual's reading fail on this
board and then confirming the working value against firmware that runs on the
same board.  Both firmware sources are described by name in the comments where
their values are used; neither contributes code, comments or structure to this
repository.

